<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Zug</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zugersee</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Zug is a lake in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, lying mostly in the canton of Zug with its southern part in Schwyz and Lucerne. The town of Zug stands on its north-eastern shore and the Rigi rises above its southern end. It linked the town with the surrounding countryside and the routes towards Lucerne and the Gotthard.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-zug.jpg" alt="Lake Zug" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robysan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aussicht_Winter_Rigi_Zugersee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
